# In the inner loop holder and key stand in front, and nothing else is to be asked there but the sum: a sum buys no loop, so the read under the key must count as something that leaves the turns, or the loop
# is built once and every turn reads twice under the text: 10,153 > 902 instructions a hundred turns, plain Bun 985 (for-in: 10,161 > 912, plain 2,729). One key bears an accessor: three turns are seven calls; the
# lie, testing=ReadsUnderKeysInFrontOfTurnsGoTheGenericRoad, makes them one.
